  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Appui au Projet Assainir Durable des Villes du Katanga - ASKAT 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ASKAT 2026 project aims to support the implementation of the Presidential Initiative &#x201c;Clean Cities&#x201d; in Lubumbashi and Kolwezi, building on the successful experience of the &#x201c;Clean Kinshasa&#x201d; model. Supported by the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands and the UN Global Compact Network, with technical assistance from the Climate &amp; Sustainability Expertise firm, the project seeks to inform the transformation the cities of Haut-Katanga and Lualaba into hubs of green, inclusive, and sustainable growth. It involves the development of Provincial and Local Sustainable Sanitation Plans (PAD &amp; PLA), the structuring of local waste recovery value chains, the strengthening of institutional capacities in line with ISO 37101, and the preparation of the Katanga Economic Forum on Sustainable Sanitation (FEAD 2026). ASKAT 2026 aspires to make Lubumbashi and Kolwezi model cities for sustainable urban sanitation in Katanga.</narrative>
  </description>
